{0 Observe Lwt}

[observe-lwt] supplies a configurable Lwt implementation of [Observe.IO.S].
It provides callback-local dynamic bindings, cleanup, and native
[Lwt.Canceled] handling, then {!val:Observe_lwt.create} completes it with a
caller-provided clock, console, and dynamic-context safety check. The latter
keeps [observe-lwt] portable: a single-threaded runtime can always allow lookup,
while a threaded composition should allow it only in the scheduler execution
context.

Use {!module:Observe_lwt.IO} with [Observe.Make] when an
application needs a custom Lwt composition. Most Lwt applications on Unix can
use the ready [observe-lwt-unix] package instead. A custom composition supplies
[sampling_draw] and [create_stable_sampling_draw] to
{!val:Observe_lwt.create}. A draw returns a finite value in the half-open
interval from zero to one, promptly. The stable factory performs no draw itself
and returns a concurrency-safe one-shot callback that invokes the source at
most once.
